What are the advantages of using Express.js with node js?
=================================================
→ Express.js provides many advantages. Some of the main advantages are:
→ Simplified web development
Express.js makes web development easy because it provides many built-in methods and features.
We do not need to write complex code for handling requests and responses like in pure Node.js.
→ Middleware support
Middleware is one of the most important features of Express.js.
Middleware handles incoming requests and outgoing responses.
It is commonly used for authentication, validation, logging, and error handling.
We can use multiple middlewares in a single application, which helps us manage a large number of requests efficiently.
→ Flexible routing system
Express.js provides a flexible and powerful routing system.
It routes incoming requests based on URLs and HTTP methods such as GET, POST, PUT, and DELETE.
Express easily understands URL patterns and maps them to the correct functions using very minimal code.
→ Template engine integration
Express.js supports template engines.
Sometimes we need to generate dynamic HTML from the Node.js API.
In such cases, template engines help us generate HTML pages dynamically on the server side.

Short interview answer (you can memorize this):
“Express.js simplifies web development in Node.js by providing built-in features like routing, middleware, and request–response handling. It reduces code, improves structure, and helps us build fast and scalable applications.”
